---
title: "Toast"
description: "Short notifications that appear in a corner and remove themselves."
tags: [feedback, accessibility, javascript]
usage: |
  Add an empty `<div class="toasts" role="status" aria-live="polite">` to the
  page, then call `showToast()`:

  ```js
  import { showToast } from "./toast.js";

  showToast("Changes saved", { variant: "success", timeout: 4000 });
  ```

  - `variant`: `info` (default), `success`, `warning` or `danger`.
  - `timeout`: milliseconds before it removes itself (default 4000).
  - `region`: the element to add it to (default the first `.toasts`).

  Set `data-animation` to `slide` (default), `fade` or `none` on the region or on
  a single toast.
accessibility: |
  - The region's `role="status"` and `aria-live="polite"` announce each toast
    without interrupting. It must be in the page before toasts are added.
  - The timer pauses while the toast is hovered. Clicking it, or pressing Enter
    or Space while it has focus, dismisses it.
  - Do not put essential information or actions only in a toast; it goes away.
  - When the person prefers reduced motion, toasts fade in and out without
    sliding.
customProperties:
  "--toasts-gap": "Space between stacked toasts."
  "--toasts-inset": "Distance of the stack from the viewport edges."
  "--toasts-z-index": "Stacking order of the region."
  "--toast-color": "Accent color; the variants set it."
  "--toast-padding": "Inner spacing."
  "--toast-radius": "Corner radius."
  "--toast-border-width": "Width of the accent border."
  "--toast-background": "Background, mixed from the accent color."
  "--toast-text-color": "Text color."
  "--toast-shadow": "Drop shadow."
  "--toast-duration": "Length of the enter and leave animation."
  "--toast-easing": "Timing function of the animation."
  "--toast-offset": "Distance the slide animation travels."
---

<link rel="stylesheet" href="./styles.css" media="screen">

<p>
  <label for="toast-animation">Animation</label>
  <select id="toast-animation">
    <option value="slide">Slide</option>
    <option value="fade">Fade</option>
    <option value="none">None</option>
  </select>
</p>

<div class="toast-demo">
  <button type="button" data-variant="info">Info toast</button>
  <button type="button" data-variant="success">Success toast</button>
  <button type="button" data-variant="warning">Warning toast</button>
  <button type="button" data-variant="danger">Danger toast</button>
</div>

<div class="toasts" role="status" aria-live="polite" data-animation="slide"></div>

<script type="module">
  import { showToast } from "./toast.js";

  const messages = {
    info: "A new version is available",
    success: "Changes saved",
    warning: "Your session expires soon",
    danger: "Could not save changes",
  };
  for (const button of document.querySelectorAll(".toast-demo button")) {
    button.addEventListener("click", () => {
      showToast(messages[button.dataset.variant], { variant: button.dataset.variant });
    });
  }
  document.getElementById("toast-animation").addEventListener("change", (event) => {
    document.querySelector(".toasts").dataset.animation = event.target.value;
  });
</script>
